       }
      ],
      "text": "Clonidine PO:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " start 0.1 mg BID (Am and bedtime); ↑ by 0.1 mg/day @ wkly intervals prn; usual 0.2–0.6 mg/day in divided doses."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "On a BB too:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " stop the BB several days b4 tapering clonidine. TCAs can blunt its effect. Watch HR w digoxin, CCBs or BBs (sinus brady). Potentiates EToH, barbiturates and other sedatives."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rebound BP rise after stopping:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " reverse w oral clonidine or IV phentolamine. OD: early HTN, then hypotension, brady, resp depression, hypothermia, drowsiness, miosis; ⍉specific antidote."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
